  "Notes": [
    {
      "Text": "Security update for stgit",
      "Title": "Topic",
      "Type": "Summary"
    },
    {
      "Text": "This update for stgit fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in stgit:\n\n- Update to version 2.7.0:\n  * Allow unambiguous command shorthands, opt-in with\n    `stgit.infer-commands`.\n  * Accept git approxidate spellings for dates, e.g. \"2 days ago\"\n    and \"@\u003cepoch\u003e\"; relative dates are now anchored in the local\n    time zone.\n  * Run `git mergetool` for `stg push` with `stgit.autoimerge`.\n  * Reject \"@\" as a branch name for `stg branch --create`.\n  * Bump gix to 0.89 and MSRV to 1.88.\n  * CVE-2026-91986: gix-transport CR/LF/NUL injection into\n    git-daemon connect request via crafted git URL path\n    (boo#1281742).\n  * CVE-2026-109349, CVE-2026-109350, CVE-2026-109351:\n    gix-pack denial of service via pack version 3 header,\n    ofs-delta base distance and pack header object count\n    (boo#1285176).\n",
      "Title": "Details",
      "Type": "General"
    },
